; TANGLE NIGHT EDGE. Program decision D10; the fifth member of the `night_edge_*` set.
;
; Matte neutral by day, an emissive Fresnel rim once `bt_darkness` rises. Every parameter of HOW
; it behaves lives in `night_edge.gdshader` -- this file overrides two colours and nothing else,
; which is why the whole set behaves identically and a tuning pass is one file rather than five.
;
; Worn by ONE mesh: the summit tread. At night the tangle is a black mass against a black sky
; and the summit bubble's glow is the only thing in it -- a bubble hanging over nothing reads as
; unreachable rather than as a reward. The rim says there is a floor under it.
[gd_resource type="ShaderMaterial" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Shader" path="res://resources/shaders/night_edge.gdshader" id="1_edge"]

[resource]
render_priority = 0
shader = ExtResource("1_edge")
; The DAYLIGHT body: the shared mid grey, as on the other four.
shader_parameter/albedo = Color(0.227, 0.227, 0.23, 1)
; The NIGHT edge: the section goal HUE at the set's shared HSV(.., 0.86, 0.85) -- the same
; construction as night_edge_{red,green,blue,cyan}, so the five differ only in hue.
shader_parameter/edge_color = Color(0.85, 0.119, 0.85, 1)
